  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The colour obtained is the colour of the compound formed in the reaction of aniline with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;followed by coupling with &beta;-naphthol.</p><p>Aniline on reaction with<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;forms a diazonium salt. This diazonium salt is then coupled with &beta;-naphthol.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/efee9b3d-987d-4749-9cef-dd50f873052c-image.png\" style=\"width: 352px; height: 270px;\" /></p>",
